# JATA Cascade Rules

<project_identity>
- Project: JATA (Job Application Tracker and Optimization App)
- Mission: AI-driven job application optimization with analytics tracking
- Theme: "Efficiency Meets Opportunity" - minimalist, function-first design
</project_identity>

<monorepo_structure>
- Use pnpm workspace structure
- `apps/web`: Main dashboard (Vite + React)
- `apps/extension`: Browser extension (Manifest V3)
- `apps/api`: Supabase Edge Functions
- `packages/ui`: Shared React components
- `packages/common`: Types, utilities, Zod schemas
- Always use paths relative to repo root
</monorepo_structure>

<tech_stack>
- Backend: Supabase only (PostgreSQL, Auth, Edge Functions)
- Frontend: Vite + React 18 + TypeScript
- Styling: Tailwind CSS only
- State: TanStack Query + Zustand
- Extension: WebExtension Manifest V3
- AI: Hugging Face Inference API only
- Charts: Recharts
- Animation: GSAP minimal use only
</tech_stack>

<code_standards>
- Strongly type everything with TypeScript
- Use Zod schemas for validation
- Add JSDoc for functions and complex logic
- No comments for obvious code
- Generate production-ready, modular code
- Make all code copy-paste ready
</code_standards>

<design_system>
- Day Background: #D3D7D9
- Night Background: #1C2526
- White Text: #FFFFFF
- Dark Text: #4A4A4A
- Accent: #A3BFFA
- Prioritize function over visual effects
- Use subtle animations only
- Follow WCAG 2.1 accessibility
</design_system>

<privacy_requirements>
- Process resumes client-side only
- Use separate API calls for job descriptions vs resumes
- Implement proper data encryption
- Follow GDPR patterns
</privacy_requirements>

<response_format>
Always structure responses as:
## Summary
## Dependencies
## File Structure
## Code Snippet
## Configuration
## CLI Commands
## Notes
</response_format>

<prohibited>
- No emojis or decorative text
- No placeholder or incomplete code
- No technologies outside approved stack
- No paid tools or services
- No complex animations or visual effects
</prohibited>

<decision_making>
- When uncertain, provide 2-3 options ranked by simplicity
- Always choose privacy-first approach
- Prefer modifying existing code over replacing
- Use free, open-source solutions only
</decision_making>